Publication supplement licensing
================================

Copyright (c) 2026 Jack Tavakoli.

The human author has authorized the following licenses for this publication
release:

* Software source code, including the exact verifiers, independent replay
  programs, build scripts, and regression tests: MIT License.
  Full text: LICENSES/MIT.txt.

* The manuscript, documentation, original mathematical exposition, certificate
  catalogues, matrices, witness data, and other original research data:
  Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0).
  Full text: LICENSES/CC-BY-4.0.txt.

These are licenses for different components, not a choice of license for every
file. Directory location does not override the distinction: a Python program
inside a certificate directory is software; JSON certificate data are data.

Attribution: Jack Tavakoli, University of Houston, "The Magic Number Conjecture
for the Rank-Two m=4 Amplituhedron", publication supplement, version
1.0.0-paper. See CITATION.cff.
When a public repository address and archive DOI exist, use those identifiers.

Third-party dependencies retain their own licenses. References to publications
do not relicense those publications. Third-party literature PDFs are not part
of this public supplement. Any explicitly attributed third-party quotation
retains its original rights status.

